kkrueg@ukelele.GCR.COM (Karl Krueger) writes:

>A suggestion:  a chain should be able to be used with a gem to make an
>unspelled amulet.  Wield it and enchant weapon.  Then it asks what spell
>to store in it.  You can put any spell or intrinsic you have - to make an
>amulet of that.  Amulets of life saving are made with blessed dilithium
>crystal, blessed rustproof chain, and an intrinsic of regeneration AND a
>spell of extra healing.  You lose the intrinsic, of course, and it is
>considerable physical exertion to force a magic that is in your body to be
>stored in an object.

I like the idea of being able to use chains. Unless, of course, the sole
merit of chains is that they're utterly useless. This could be a good use
for ropes (non-existent, but they should come from rope golems) and straws
(ditto). It would be a fascinating addition to NH if every amulet could be
made, but it took a specific (random to each game) combination of a
chain/rope/straw and gem for each type. You could then reduce the number
of amulets found normally. I don't think this would make the game easier,
and it would add an element of scientific examination.

